I teach statistics at undergraduate, master’s and doctoral level, combining statistical reasoning, applications and reproducible data analysis.

## Current and recent courses

- **Social and Health Statistics**, PhD in Public Administration, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice and University of Milano-Bicocca.
- **R Coding and Finance Analytics**, MSc in Economics, Finance and Sustainability, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice.
- **Statistics 1 — practice classes**, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice.
- **Experimental Design and Statistical Analysis**, MSc in Marine Biology, University of Padova.
- **Statistical Models 1 and 2 — laboratory classes**, University of Padova.

## Thesis supervision

I am available to supervise bachelor’s and master’s theses with a substantial statistical component. Relevant topics include health inequalities, environment and health, population ageing, sport analytics, Bayesian statistics, time-series models and interpretable machine learning.
